    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0951" n="845" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg845"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">192/1672: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-08-26T13:00:00+03:00">August 26, 1939—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 26—8:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>474. The Foreign Office states that the Soviet steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kim</hi> sailed from Leningrad on August 9 en route to Vladivostok and is
                    due to arrive in the Panama Canal Zone in about 4 days but is not in possession
                    of bill of health for the reason that instructions from Amtorg<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d657-f1"/> regarding the new regulations requiring such bills of
                        health<anchor n="51" xml:id="d657-f2"/> were not received in Moscow until
                    August 25. The Foreign Office will appreciate having the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kim</hi> permitted to pass through the Canal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d657-f1" n="50" xml:id="d657-f1-content">
                <p>Amtorg Trading Corporation, official purchasing and sales agency in the United
                    States of the Soviet Union, 261 Fifth Avenue, New York, N. Y.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d657-f2" n="51" xml:id="d657-f2-content">
                <p>Certain amendments and additions to the Rules and Regulations Governing
                    Navigation of the Panama Canal and Adjacent Waters were made effective on August
                    15, 1939, by The Panama Canal, Executive Office, Balboa Heights, C. Z., C. S.
                    Ridley, Governor.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
